v> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds really awesome, honestly. Travelling to other realms and learning more about them has always been a favorite of mine in mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:16:46-07:00","id":1131149,"title":"","content":"Correction - the book is called <b>Fallen Worlds</b>. The plural is important.<br /> <br /> It's Awakening's Shadow, Underworld, Lower Depths, and other strange places book. We've had it scheduled for years, but for obvious reasons couldn't actually <i>do</i> it until Geist and Changeling second editions were written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:25:20-07:00","id":1131151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131149#post1131149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction - the book is called <b>Fallen Worlds</b>. The plural is important.<br /> <br /> It's Awakening's Shadow, Underworld, Lower Depths, and other strange places book. We've had it scheduled for years, but for obvious reasons couldn't actually <i>do</i> it until Geist and Changeling second editions were written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that because Mages consider the Hedge and Changeling Arcadia to be part of the Lower Depths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:26:44-07:00","id":1131152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131151#post1131151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that because Mages consider the Hedge and Changeling Arcadia to be part of the Lower Depths?</div> </div> </div> </div>or as &quot;other strange places&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:54:16-07:00","id":1131155,"title":"","content":"I reserve judgement until I see the C2e hedge, frankly.<br /> <br /> This book will finally let us show the Shadow from a Spirit Mage's point of view - if you read the 1e Shadow, it's tinged differently to Werewolf or mortal/book of spirits, and Werewolf sometimes makes mention of mages doing very weird things from the uratha's perspective. Don't expect a werewolf crossover, do expect to be mapping Places That Aren't or voyaging into the Shadow's sky with the Thrice-Great.<br /> <br /> And extend that &quot;fresh perspective on a shared setting space&quot; to the Underworld and established Lower Depths like Inferno, too.<br /> <br /> To see the opposite in action, wait for the Beast Player's guide, which details the astral realms from the Begotten's (very different to mages) perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T01:56:58-07:00","id":1131164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131155#post1131155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reserve judgement until I see the C2e hedge, frankly.<br /> <br /> This book will finally let us show the Shadow from a Spirit Mage's point of view - if you read the 1e Shadow, it's tinged differently to Werewolf or mortal/book of spirits, and Werewolf sometimes makes mention of mages doing very weird things from the uratha's perspective. Don't expect a werewolf crossover, do expect to be mapping Places That Aren't or voyaging into the Shadow's sky with the Thrice-Great.<br /> <br /> And extend that &quot;fresh perspective on a shared setting space&quot; to the Underworld and established Lower Depths like Inferno, too.<br /> <br /> To see the opposite in action, wait for the Beast Player's guide, which details the astral realms from the Begotten's (very different to mages) perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Related question: Will Deviant have any substantive connection to the established otherworlds or its own special setting dimension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T01:56:58-07:00","id":1131165,"title":"","content":"Deleted-Double Post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:01:28-07:00","id":1131189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131155#post1131155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reserve judgement until I see the C2e hedge, frankly.<br /> <br /> This book will finally let us show the Shadow from a Spirit Mage's point of view - if you read the 1e Shadow, it's tinged differently to Werewolf or mortal/book of spirits, and Werewolf sometimes makes mention of mages doing very weird things from the uratha's perspective. Don't expect a werewolf crossover, do expect to be mapping Places That Aren't or voyaging into the Shadow's sky with the Thrice-Great.<br /> <br /> And extend that &quot;fresh perspective on a shared setting space&quot; to the Underworld and established Lower Depths like Inferno, too.<br /> <br /> To see the opposite in action, wait for the Beast Player's guide, which details the astral realms from the Begotten's (very different to mages) perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much differently would the Underworld be from Mage perspective compared to a Sin-Eater perspective? (Then again I suppose a Geist itself could be their bound's effective tour guide)<br /> <br /> Is the Athenaeum still a place in 2e? I imagine it would be one of the more useful Underworld locations to a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:18:55-07:00","id":1131196,"title":"","content":"I'm going to pray to the Onyx Path developer gods really hard for Legacy write-ups of House Vedmak or the Hollow Keepers. They're both some pretty long shots, but I'm too mechanically creative stupid to make one about exploring other worlds but stealing or manipulating souls to do so, so I'd love it in a book that's, you know, about exploring other worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member"