4_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:05:57-07:00","id":1131223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131189#post1131189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much differently would the Underworld be from Mage perspective compared to a Sin-Eater perspective? (Then again I suppose a Geist itself could be their bound's effective tour guide)<br /> <br /> Is the Athenaeum still a place in 2e? I imagine it would be one of the more useful Underworld locations to a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with the Shadow, mages shortcut the major difficulty in navigating the Underworld with the rest of their Arcana. Werewolves and Bound both &quot;fit in&quot; to the rules of &quot;their&quot; realms. Mages don't, and have none of the protections afforded a semi-native, but mages ignore rules when it suits them.<br /> <br /> The Shadow's sky is mysterious to uratha despite having a celestial spirit as a creator because they can't fly, and any spirit capable of giving them a lift is pushed down by Helios' singular presence. A Forces/Spirit legacy like the Thrice-Great say &quot;fuck yo gravity&quot; and go deal with the spirit courts of the night sky. (this is, of course, very dangerous. There's idigam up there).<br /> <br /> The underworld's like that, in different ways. Can't give examples until Geist is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:11:45-07:00","id":1131226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131223#post1131223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As with the Shadow, mages shortcut the major difficulty in navigating the Underworld with the rest of their Arcana. Werewolves and Bound both &amp;quot;fit in&amp;quot; to the rules of &amp;quot;their&amp;quot; realms. Mages don't, and have none of the protections afforded a semi-native, but mages ignore rules when it suits them.<br /> <br /> The Shadow's sky is mysterious to uratha despite having a celestial spirit as a creator because they can't fly, and any spirit capable of giving them a lift is pushed down by Helios' singular presence. A Forces/Spirit legacy like the Thrice-Great say &amp;quot;fuck yo gravity&amp;quot; and go deal with the spirit courts of the night sky. (this is, of course, very dangerous. There's idigam up there).<br /> <br /> The underworld's like that, in different ways. Can't give examples until Geist is out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doesn't that risk Mages being better in other gamelines sandboxes then they, what sort of disadvantages does a Mage have in the Shadow compared to a Werewolf for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:28:53-07:00","id":1131232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131226#post1131226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that risk Mages being better in other gamelines sandboxes then they, what sort of disadvantages does a Mage have in the Shadow compared to a Werewolf for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>As he just said, Mages aren't protected by having any &quot;native&quot; status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:31:53-07:00","id":1131236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\">