 Shadow from a Spirit Mage's point of view - if you read the 1e Shadow, it's tinged differently to Werewolf or mortal/book of spirits, and Werewolf sometimes makes mention of mages doing very weird things from the uratha's perspective. Don't expect a werewolf crossover, do expect to be mapping Places That Aren't or voyaging into the Shadow's sky with the Thrice-Great.<br /> <br /> And extend that &amp;quot;fresh perspective on a shared setting space&amp;quot; to the Underworld and established Lower Depths like Inferno, too.<br /> <br /> To see the opposite in action, wait for the Beast Player's guide, which details the astral realms from the Begotten's (very different to mages) perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will we see mages Interact interesse with inferno demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:50:42-07:00","id":1131274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131155#post1131155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To see the opposite in action, wait for the Beast Player's guide, which details the astral realms from the Begotten's (very different to mages) perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Fallen Worlds also going to have a section on the Astral? Because I looooooove the Steve Ditko Astral shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:05:26-07:00","id":1131299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131232#post1131232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As he just said, Mages aren't protected by having any &quot;native&quot; status.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; Spirits may react to Uratha like your typical citizen going &quot;Fucking pigs&quot; but a lone mage may actually be regarded like possible prey. And without the proper protections (such as throwing a mage not versed on the Spirit Arcanum into the Shadow) it's only a matter of time before some spirit realizes they're ripe for possession; or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:15:43-07:00","id":1131306,"title":"","content":"If there's idigam where they're going, they're in for some fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:23:31-07:00","id":1131310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131223#post1131223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Forces/Spirit legacy like the Thrice-Great say &quot;fuck yo gravity&quot; and go deal with the spirit courts of the night sky. (this is, of course, very dangerous. There's idigam up there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking about Legacies and books, are we going to see in this book -or the other 2 we know about- more 1st Ed Mage Legacies translated into 2Ed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:57:51-07:00","id":1131326,"title":"","content":"I personally hope not, original content is usually more interesting and with the rules given converting the legacy mechanics for the first edition legacies is quite doable so that I'd rather see a new legacy or two dealing with the otherworlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:04:54-07:00","id":1131329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131299#post1131299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed; Spirits may react to Uratha like your typical citizen going &quot;Fucking pigs&quot; but a lone mage may actually be regarded like possible prey. And without the proper protections (such as throwing a mage not versed on the Spirit Arcanum into the Shadow) it's only a matter of time before some spirit realizes they're ripe for possession; or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most Arcana are not only more that capable of defending a mage in the Shadow, but causing havoc to the local ecology.<br /> <br /> I believe that once local spirits realize the human is a mage, they're viewed as very dangerous imperialists, bullies, warlords and interlopers that could easily upset the delicate balance of spirit politics and hierarchy, sort of like a British general or industrialist in late 19th Century India.<br /> <br /> Edit: The dimensional imperialist view would also be very consistent with Mage's themes of power, extreme privilege and lack of consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-19-2017, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:08:33-07:00","id":1131330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131155#post1131155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reserve judgement until I see the C2e hedge, frankly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to long ago you indicated that Changeling Arcadia and the Hedge are definitely part of the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Has OPP potentially mage such significant changes to Changeling 2e since the departure of David Hill as developer that this might no longer be the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:15:31-07:00","id":1131334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131310#post1131310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking about Legacies and books, are we going to see in this book -or the other 2 we know about- more 1st Ed Mage Legacies translated into 2Ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's been said that SoS has no room for a legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:38:49-07:00","id":1131350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131261#post1131261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you want to see this argument go on and on, then go to 4chan /tg /CofD/ &amp; /wodg/ Chronicles of Darkness and World of Darkness General<br /> <br /> You will see threads and threads about Mage supremacy, its already a thing and frankly stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not claiming Mage Supremacy, but to avoid such future head aches it'd be nice if it was clearer what native protections/advantages are compared to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:41:21-07:00","id":1131351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131237#post1131237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an entirely serious question, and I need to clarify that because I know how it's going to sound:<br /> <br /> Why does that matter? Like all arguments about whether or not Mages are better in these spaces than the natives aside, why is that problematic?</div> </div> </div> </div>On a very clear day, with a powerful telescope, I can glimpse how much I care about that.<br /> <br /> As others have correctly guessed, the major theme of Fallen Worlds is that mages are <i>intruding</i> on these worlds. They don't belong, and they disrupt them by being there. Mages try to buy their way into spirit courts' graces by creating essence, and end up making magath in the process. They punch holes in the gauntlet for their own convenience. Even the most conscientious Thyrsus s warping the Shadow by his presence, and spirits *resent* it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:49:29-07:00","id":1131355,"title":"","content":"Among the Fallen Worlds, unlike the Shadow, Underworld and Hedge, aren't mages considered at least considered &quot;semi-native&quot; in the Astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T11:47:32-07:00","id":1131367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131351#post1131351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a very clear day, with a powerful telescope, I can glimpse how much I care about that.<br /> <br /> As others have correctly guessed, the major theme of Fallen Worlds is that mages are <i>intruding</i> on these worlds. They don't belong, and they disrupt them by being there. Mages try to buy their way into spirit courts' graces by creating essence, and end up making magath in the process. They punch holes in the gauntlet for their own convenience. Even the most conscientious Thyrsus s warping the Shadow by his presence, and spirits *resent* it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh so mages are the Bull in a China shop, they're like the eco tourists that damage the very natural areas they are curious about.<br /> <br /> Of man are Mages going to be the Splat other Splats hate, if only because the other splats have to clean up after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T11:48:43-07:00","id":1131368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131351#post1131351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a very clear day, with a powerful telescope, I can glimpse how much I care about that.<br /> <br /> As others have correctly guessed, the major theme of Fallen Worlds is that mages are <i>intruding</i> on these worlds. They don't belong, and they disrupt them by being there. Mages try to buy their way into spirit courts' graces by creating essence, and end up making magath in the process. They punch holes in the gauntlet for their own convenience. Even the most conscientious Thyrsus s warping the Shadow by his presence, and spirits *resent* it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, I understand now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:06:52-07:00","id":1131375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131329#post1131329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Most Arcana are not only more that capable of defending a mage in the Shadow, but causing havoc to the local ecology.<br /> <br /> I believe that once local spirits realize the human is a mage, they're viewed as very dangerous imperialists, bullies, warlords and interlopers that could easily upset the delicate balance of spirit politics and hierarchy, sort of like a British general or industrialist in late 19th Century India.<br /> <br /> Edit: The dimensional imperialist view would also be very consistent with Mage's themes of power, extreme privilege and lack of consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of imagination is beyond the intellectual scope of 90% of all spirits.<br /> <br /> At least Uratha were <i>made</i> to hunt and cull spirits. A rank 2 spirit isn't going to care for a mage's &quot;imperialistic views&quot;, it'll care that they're shifting the power balance which it found it's niche on. Even if they won't be able to put those views into concise communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-19-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:10:05-07:00","id":1131376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131355#post1131355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the Fallen Worlds, unlike the Shadow, Underworld and Hedge, aren't mages considered at least considered &amp;quot;semi-native&amp;quot; in the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so. You pretty much need the Mind arcanum to do anything there, so I believe that still makes them count as invaders.<br /> <br /> I believe that the natives of the Astral Realms are goetia (obviously) and Beasts. These two groups have an innate connection that is deeper than any Mage's when it comes to the Astral Realms.<br /> <br /> On a side note, are we going to see little blurbs on how the other splats would feel about this invasiveness like 1000 years of night had little blurbs about the other splats, or is it primarily going to be stuff like the Goetia, Spirits, and Ghosts in this case?<br /> <br /> Also, I know that the Inferno and whatever shadowy world the Strix originally came from count as lower depths, but what other ones are there? I'm not as well versed in mage as the other lines, so it'd be pretty neat to look at a 1e book with this stuff in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:13:06-07:00","id":1131377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131355#post1131355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the Fallen Worlds, unlike the Shadow, Underworld and Hedge, aren't mages considered at least considered &quot;semi-native&quot; in the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>In as much as every human being has a representation there and are influenced by it. But Mages can also influence it themselves, which set them apart from your common folk. Imagine if the concept of social Darwinism was born off a Mastigos messing in the astral with particular views on how societies should work? Sounds feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:22:42-07:00","id":1131386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131376#post1131376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You pretty much need the Mind arcanum to do anything there.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Arcana function fine in the Astral, and you don't even need Mind to enter the realm.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:40:06-07:00","id":1131389,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Shadow diseases from Book of Spirits will be mentioned? They're probably fairly easily dealt with (especially by a Thyrsus), but they certainly give the impression that a mage shouldn't really be in the Shadow, and there's always the odd chance that a mage gets lazy and accidently ends up in a coma or something.<br /> <br /> Also, having the Spirit Arcana cause what amounts to environmental damage to the Gauntlet is a really interesting way to address the comparative ease with which the Awakened can cross when compared to the Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:50:53-07:00","id":1131392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131389#post1131389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, having the Spirit Arcana cause what amounts to environmental damage to the Gauntlet is a really interesting way to address the comparative ease with which the Awakened can cross when compared to the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, stuff any spirit with Gateway into a fetish and you can do the same while scaring pesky spirits out of your way. That or get some corpus off such a spirit for a talen with the same capabilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:53:26-07:00","id":1131393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131392#post1131392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah, stuff any spirit with Gateway into a fetish and you can do the same while scaring pesky spirits out of your way.</div> </div> </div> </div>'The location has a hole punched through the Gauntlet. Spirits, packs \u2014 and even incautious humans \u2014 can cross through it without the use of any powers. The Shadow Gate is visible even to material beings, as the Shadow world and material worlds mix.'<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img1.stewmac.com/product/images/33059/w_440/h_440/Fret_Fingerboard_Levelers.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:00:41-07:00","id":1131396,"title":"","content":"Reading all this, is there *any* way for a mage to actually get along well with spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:06:06-07:00","id":1131398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131396#post1131396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading all this, is there *any* way for a mage to actually get along well with spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind Spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:06:06-07:00","id":1131399,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of ways. Though getting along well with <i>all </i>spirits is probably impossible. Even if you just stand there sharing Essence there's going to be spirits feeling left out, or annoyed that you're bloating weak spirits.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that whenever things become 'unbalanced' that only one side is going to get annoyed by it. When a mage kicks over a spirit of authoritarianism, the spirit of anarchy its been keeping down gets an opportunity. The problem is that there's a lot of ripples.<br /> <br /> I don't expect there would be a realistic, 'All spirits love me' end game, if that's what you mean. But you can get lots of spirits to 'like' you by helping them do what they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:07:26-07:00","id":1131401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131386#post1131386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All Arcana function fine in the Astral, and you don't even need Mind to enter the realm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought you needed the Mind Arcana to actually get there because I don't remember any Astral Irises existing. How does a person get there then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:10:40-07:00","id":1131403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131401#post1131401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I thought you needed the Mind Arcana to actually get there because I don't remember any Astral Irises existing. How does a person get there then?</div> </div> </div> </div>'In addition, a mage may travel to the Astral Realms from a Demesne (but not a natural Verge) powered by her own soul stone, a stone with a soul on the same Path, or through any Path\u2019s stone (with the permission of the sorcerer whose soul resides within it). Once given, permission cannot be rescinded until the beneficiary returns.'<br /> <br /> There are also Astral Irises, called Synesi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:13:03-07:00","id":1131405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131401#post1131401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I thought you needed the Mind Arcana to actually get there because I don't remember any Astral Irises existing. How does a person get there then?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally all covered in the corebook's section on the Astral.<br /> <br /> You meditate in a Hallow or a Demesne or \u2014 yes, they do exist \u2014 fulfill the Key of one of the Astral Irises known as Synesi, and from there you form an Astral Path and enter your Oneiros or the Iris's destination realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:22:19-07:00","id":1131411,"title":"","content":"Of course I'm not na\u00efve enough to believe in a &quot;Shadow utopia&quot; being possible just by trying to be nice to Spirits, it's more of a question of whether the Mage can create a sort of a new equilibrium. No problem with an Anarchy Spirit, when one &quot;takes care&quot; of the Spirit in question and keeps things stable, especially if they clean up the material side of the Gauntlet as well.<br /> <br /> And I don't think that Mind magic would win any real friends and it would piss off a lot of uncontrolled Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:26:33-07:00","id":1131415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131376#post1131376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe so. You pretty much need the Mind arcanum to do anything there, so I believe that still makes them count as invaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need Mind to operate in the Astral, and Mages are one of the only splats that can enter the Astral without the use of powers beyond expending some mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:29:21-07:00","id":1131418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131392#post1131392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah, stuff any spirit with Gateway into a fetish and you can do the same while scaring pesky spirits out of your way. That or get some corpus off such a spirit for a talen with the same capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you're still messing around with items. By default, the Uratha generally need a locus when entering or leaving the Shadow. A starting Thyrsus can just open a portal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:33:16-07:00","id":1131420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131405#post1131405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally all covered in the corebook's section on the Astral.<br /> <br /> You meditate in a Hallow or a Demesne or \u2014 yes, they do exist \u2014 fulfill the Key of one of the Astral Irises known as Synesi, and from there you form an Astral Path and enter your Oneiros or the Iris's destination realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mage group hasn't really done anything with the Astral, so I haven't really read anything about it since I once gave it a cursory glance. I just figured you'd need Mind Magic for it because we haven't done anything with it.<br /> <br /> The only other game I was in that dealt with the Astral in anyway I was playing a vampire, so I really never learned much about it since I was pretty much incapable of accessing any of the realms with ephemeral entities, and I was typically discouraged from doing anything with them without having a mage with me and my character never really got to do anything with mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:33:25-07:00","id":1131421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131411#post1131411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I'm not na\u00efve enough to believe in a &quot;Shadow utopia&quot; being possible just by trying to be nice to Spirits, it's more of a question of whether the Mage can create a sort of a new equilibrium. No problem with an Anarchy Spirit, when one &quot;takes care&quot; of the Spirit in question and keeps things stable, especially if they clean up the material side of the Gauntlet as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with that is that these actions have ripples that don't limit things to their choir. So you get rid of the oppressing spirit and now the law and order spirits aren't as strong. And the anarchy spirit may be willing to work with you, but the crime and chaos spirits are busy enjoying the break from the tyranny and are causing all sorts of disorder. Now rather than overextend their authority, police are more likely to flat out break the law, giving into bribes and outright helping criminal organizations. Weather patterns are acting weird. The order spirits have been pushed to starvation and start eating other things, and spirits say magath and the mage thinks they're talking about MAGA. And so on and so on.<br /> <br /> It's an ecosystem. Except instead of bees and molds and wolves and eagles you have predatory beings of ephemera that can be inspired to leap across and start merging with souls.<br /> <br /> There is an archmage who's trying to create an equilibrium in the books, his name is Theumiel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131424#post1131424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group hasn't really done anything with Demenses and Soul stones, so I haven't looked at all their rule yet.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I should'be figured the Astral had irises, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't either, which is fortunate since someone's about to get Prelacy. Don't feel too bad it's a big book and there's a lot in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:34:47-07:00","id":1131422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131411#post1131411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Mage can create a sort of a new equilibrium.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not too Hubristic!<br /> <br /> But sure, the mage can certainly just bring civilization and order to those savage spirits. He's a damn mage, he knows what's best for the Shadow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What could go wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:36:24-07:00","id":1131424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131403#post1131403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'In addition, a mage may travel to the Astral Realms from a Demesne (but not a natural Verge) powered by her own soul stone, a stone with a soul on the same Path, or through any Path\u2019s stone (with the permission of the sorcerer whose soul resides within it). Once given, permission cannot be rescinded until the beneficiary returns.'<br /> <br /> There are also Astral Irises, called Synesi.</div> </div> </div> </div>My group hasn't really done anything with Demenses and Soul stones, so I haven't looked at all their rule yet.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I should'be figured the Astral had irises, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:38:38-07:00","id":1131426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131424#post1131424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My group hasn't really done anything with Demenses and Soul stones, so I haven't looked at all their rule yet.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I should'be figured the Astral had irises, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget that as another poster mentioned, a mage only needs a Hallow and some mana to meditate into the Astral. <br /> <br /> Mage 2e rules are clearly designed for all mages to have ready access, not just Mastigos or high experience/resource cabals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:39:44-07:00","id":1131427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131422#post1131422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not too Hubristic!<br /> <br /> But sure, the mage can certainly just bring civilization and order to those savage spirits. He's a damn mage, he knows what's best for the Shadow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What could go wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;B- But I had to do something! The city was in chaos and I had to act! I had no other choice!! Can't you SEE?! Why won't you understand?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>- Stereotypical &quot;excuse&quot; often heard at Consilium meetings</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-19-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:10:49-07:00","id":1131435,"title":"","content":"I think Sanctum and Sigil mentions some special 'other world' rules consilium have so they can call out when someone's messing things up or when the shadow's extra dangerous.<br /> <br /> It's not always going to end in city-shattering events, of course. You stop the river spirit from its habit of taking one life every year, and some wells dry up a few miles away and farms go under. A rampant joy spirit at a playground was making people go crazy and you lock it away and now no kids go there and it's just a hangout for drug dealers and home for the homeless. The spirit of your sanctum gets too full of itself so you disperse it and now it takes a few extra minutes to get started with the day or rituals because you can never remember where you put everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:45:12-07:00","id":1131481,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131393#post1131393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'The location has a hole punched through the Gauntlet. Spirits, packs \u2014 and even incautious humans \u2014 can cross through it without the use of any powers. The Shadow Gate is visible even to material beings, as the Shadow world and material worlds mix.'<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your fetish doesn't needs to copy exact spirit traits. It's obvious a spirit with gateway can make doorways into the shadow, but put it on a skeleton key and use it on a literal doorway and all you have to do is close the way behind you. Wouldn't be as easy with a talen, mind.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:51:28-07:00","id":1131513,"title":"","content":"I assume we're talking about Werewolf fetishes (or Homebrew), because Mage fetishes don't hold Manifestations, which is what Shadow Gate is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}